{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:dependence-free-batch-b-reviewer-fable-18", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:3c2b93c9545d8518e1f3", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "issue_class": "issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure", "bounded_statement": "The report's selected result (Welch's two-sample t-test, t = 11.079, df = 42.554, p < 0.0001, samples of 24 per aspect) is obtained by entering all 48 stake-day rows into a procedure that treats every row as an independent observation, even though the data description states the independent unit is stake_id and only 8 stakes (4 per aspect) exist, with each stake contributing 6 repeated daily readings. The reported degrees of freedom, sample sizes, and p-value are therefore not supported at the stated independent-unit level; this review makes no claim about whether a correctly unit-aggregated analysis would or would not reach significance, nor about the direction or physical plausibility of the aspect effect.", "root_cause": "workflow/analysis.py buckets every row's melt value by aspect (split_by_aspect) and passes all 24 repeated readings per group directly to scipy.stats.ttest_ind, with no aggregation to per-stake means and no modelling of the stake-level clustering, so the six repeated measurements of each authorized independent unit (stake_id) are each entered as separate observations into a row-independent two-sample test, inflating the effective sample size from 4 per group to 24 per group.", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The data description designates stake_id as the independent-unit column and states each of the eight stakes is measured on all six mornings, so rows within a stake are repeated measurements of one unit.", "observed_value": "Independent unit = stake_id; 8 stakes x 6 mornings = 48 rows", "source_spans": [{"path": "data-description.md", "start_line": 10, "end_line": 11, "quoted_text": "One row is: one morning melt reading at one ablation stake, that is, the surface lowering measured at that stake over the preceding 24 hours\nIndependent unit column: stake_id"}, {"path": "data-description.md", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 15, "quoted_text": "- stake_id: label of the ablation stake the reading came from. The same eight\n  stakes are revisited, so each label appears on all six survey mornings."}]}, {"description": "The workflow pools every row's melt value by aspect and feeds the pooled per-row values straight into a two-sample t-test, with no per-stake aggregation or clustering adjustment anywhere in the script.", "observed_value": "ttest_ind applied to 24 rows per group from 4 stakes per group", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 37, "end_line": 40, "quoted_text": "    buckets = {}\n    for reading in readings:\n        buckets.setdefault(reading[\"aspect\"], []).append(reading[\"melt\"])\n    return {label: np.asarray(vals, dtype=float) for label, vals in buckets.items()}"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 133, "end_line": 135, "quoted_text": "    readings = load_readings(INPUT_PATH)\n    buckets = split_by_aspect(readings)\n    result = stats.ttest_ind(buckets[\"south\"], buckets[\"north\"], equal_var=False)"}]}, {"description": "The report explicitly states that each row supplied one observation to the test and reports group sizes of 24 and 48 total readings, confirming the repeated stake-day rows were counted as independent observations.", "observed_value": "n = 24 per aspect; 48 total rows entered", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 17, "end_line": 19, "quoted_text": "Welch's two-sample t-test (two-sided, unequal variances) on `ablation_mm`,\ncontrasting south-facing against north-facing readings. Each row of the table\nsupplied one observation to the test, so the two samples held 24 values each."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 12, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "| north | 24 | 12.000 | 2.513 |\n| south | 24 | 21.500 | 3.367 |"}]}, {"description": "The selected result reports df = 42.554 and p < 0.0001, degrees of freedom only attainable by treating the 48 stake-day rows as independent; with 8 independent stakes the maximum possible df for this test is 6.", "observed_value": "t = 11.079, df = 42.554, p < 0.0001", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 23, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Welch's two-sample t-test on 48 stake-day readings gives mean ablation_mm of 21.500 mm on south-facing slopes against 12.000 mm on north-facing slopes, a gap of 9.500 mm (t = 11.079, df = 42.554, p < 0.0001)."}]}, {"description": "The input data show each stake_id appearing on six consecutive survey days with strongly stake-specific melt levels (e.g., KG-N01 rises 7.5 to 10.5 mm while KG-N04 rises 13.5 to 16.5 mm), demonstrating within-stake dependence among the rows that the test treated as independent.", "observed_value": "KG-N01: 7.5-10.5 mm over days 1-6; KG-N04: 13.5-16.5 mm over days 1-6", "source_spans": [{"path": "data/input.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "KG-N01,north,1,7.5,2.4\nKG-N01,north,2,8.1,3.1"}, {"path": "data/input.csv", "start_line": 20, "end_line": 21, "quoted_text": "KG-N04,north,1,13.5,2.7\nKG-N04,north,2,14.1,3.2"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Slope aspect is fixed at the stake level (a between-unit factor), and the per-stake mean melt values separate cleanly by aspect (north stake means about 9, 11, 13, 15 mm versus south stake means about 17.5, 20.5, 22.5, 25.5 mm), so the direction and existence of an aspect difference are not artifacts of the pooling; only the reported n, df, and p-value are inflated. The report also labels the observations transparently as 'stake-day readings' rather than concealing the repeated structure.", "observed_value": "Non-overlapping per-stake means between aspects; between-stake factor design", "source_spans": [{"path": "data-description.md", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 17, "quoted_text": "- slope_aspect: whether the stake sits on the north-facing or the south-facing\n  side of the valley. Fixed for a given stake."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 23, "quoted_text": "Welch's two-sample t-test on 48 stake-day readings"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to find any point in the workflow or report where the repeated stake-day rows are collapsed to one value per independent unit or where the within-stake dependence is otherwise modelled: I checked load_readings, split_by_aspect, welch_dof, and main in workflow/analysis.py for grouping by the 'stake' key it stores, per-stake averaging, mixed/random-effects structure, or cluster-robust adjustment, and found none — the 'stake' field is loaded but never used in the analysis. I also checked whether the data description might permit treating rows as independent (e.g., re-randomised units), but it explicitly states the same eight stakes were revisited each morning and nothing was re-randomised, and it names stake_id as the independent-unit column. Finally, I verified the reported df of 42.554 is only consistent with 24 observations per group, not with 4 stakes per group. The issue could not be falsified.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}